 fact, as Peter Ackroyd points out, \"His private choices and obsessions became emblematic of, and in some sense determined our understanding of, the twentieth-century tradition.\" Eliot insisted on the importance of literary tradition, yet he had no real predecessors or successors. Along with Pound, Joyce, and Woolf, he helped give birth to modernism in literature, but then later in his career he abandoned it.","publicationYear":1984,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-t-s-eliot-peter-ackroyd"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"American Poets","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-t-s-eliot-peter-ackroyd"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Eliot, T. S. (Thomas Stearns), 1888-1965","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-t-s-eliot-peter-ackroyd"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"American Authors","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-t-s-eliot-peter-ackroyd"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biographies","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-t-s-eliot-peter-ackroyd"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Poètes américains","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-t-s-eliot-peter-ackroyd"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biografie","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-t-s-eliot-peter-ackroyd"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Poets","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-t-s-eliot-peter-ackroyd"}],"displaySummary":"This is only one of a number of paradoxes in Eliot's life. Perhaps chief among them, as this biography demonstrates, was Eliot's insistence on the impersonality of great poetry while at the same time his own work was suffused with his experience and personality. In fact, as Peter Ackroyd points out, \"His private choices and o